{"strongs": "H3577", "word": "כָּזָב", "translit": "ka.zav", "root": "כזב", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "lie, falsehood, deceptive thing", "definition": "כָּזָב noun masculine Amos 2:4 lie, falsehood, deceptive thing ; — absolute ׳ כ Hos 12:2 + 19 t.; plural absolute כְּזָבִים Judg 16:10 + 9 t.; suffix כִּזְבֵיהֶם Amos 2:4 — lie, falsehood , with דִּבֶּר Judg 16:10 ; Judg 16:13 ; Hos 7:13 ; Zeph 3:13 ; Dan 11:27 ; Ps 5:7 ; Ps 58:4 , so Ezek 13:8 Co (by transposing ׳ כ with שָׁוְא , compare v Ezek 13:6 v Ezek 13:7 v Ezek 13:9 ); with יָפִיחַ (in Proverbs) Prov 6:19 ; Prov 14:5 ; Prov 14:25 ; Prov 19:5 ; Prov 19:9 of false prophecies (divinations) with אָמַר , ׳ מִקְסַם כ Ezek 13:7 with קָסַם v Ezek 13:9 ; Ezek 21:34 ; Ezek 22:28 + Ezek 13:6 ᵐ5 Co ( ׳ קָסוֺם כ , for ᵑ0 ׳ קֶסֶם כ ); with שָׁמַע Ezek 13:19 , בִּקֵּשׁ Ps 4:3 with רָצָה delight in Ps 62:5 so in the phrase ׳ דְּבַרכֿ Prov 30:8 , ׳ אִישׁ כ Prov 19:22 = liar , עֵד כְּזָבִים Prov 21:28 = false witness ; of idols. as a lie ( res ementita ) Amos 2:4 , so probably ׳ שָׂטֵי כ those turning aside to a lie Ps 40:5 (compare אָוֶן , אֱלִיל , הֶבֶל , שֶׁקֶר ); then of empty human pretensions וָשֹׁד יַרְבֶּה ׳ כ Hos 12:2 ; Isa 28:15 (|| שֶׁקֶר ), v Isa 28:17 ( ׳ מַחְסֵה כ ), Ps 62:10 (|| הֶבֶל ; compare כֹּזֵב Ps 116:11 ); לֶחֶם כְּזָבִים Prov 23:3 = deceptive (disappointing) bread .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3976')\">BDB3976</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3577')\">H3577</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3975')\">BDB3975</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3977')\">BDB3977</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>כָּזָב</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Amos 2:4\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(30,2,4)\">Amos 2:4</ref></sup> <highlightword>lie, falsehood, deceptive thing</highlightword>; — absolute <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>כ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Hos 12:2\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"12\" vBeg